This JavaScript function should return the n-th Fibonacci number (fib(0) = 0, fib(1) = 1) but it is wrong for n = 0 and far too slow for n = 80. Fix it and explain the change in two sentences.

```js
function fib(n) {
  if (n <= 1) return 1;
  return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
}
```
